Appendix A wide selection-ന്റെ നിർബന്ധിത `N=M^2+1` boundary exact arithmetic-ോടെ പരിശോധിക്കുന്ന clean Stage 1 probe. stream first=1, directionStep=+1; places=3, digits 0,1,2, wide=1+M+2M^2. wide acceptance limit-ിനുള്ളിലാണ്; expected rank M-1 ആണ്.

Hamlet, M സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Juliet, N=M squared plus 1 സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Romeo, space=M cubed സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Othello, wide value സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Macbeth, acceptance limit സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Lady Macbeth, final rank സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ophelia, M നിർമ്മിക്കാൻ doubling count സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Prospero, flow-വും assignment-വും സഹായിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.

Act I: M നിർമ്മിക്കുന്നു.

Scene I: one, count 127.
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero:
 You are a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between a big big big big big big big hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Hamlet and Ophelia]

Scene II: doubling loop.
Hamlet:
 Are you better than nothing?
Ophelia:
 If not, let us proceed to scene III.
Hamlet:
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
Ophelia:
 You are as good as the product of yourself and a big hero.
 Let us return to scene II.

Scene III: M=2 power 127 minus 1.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.

Act II: wide space-വും value-വും.

Scene I: N=M squared plus 1.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Juliet]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the product of Hamlet and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: places=3 ആയതിനാൽ space=M cubed.
[Enter Prospero and Romeo]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the product of Hamlet and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the product of yourself and Hamlet.
[Exeunt]

Scene III: first=1, step plus one എന്ന answer ring-ന്റെ digits 0,1,2 ഉപയോഗിച്ച് wide=1+M+2M squared.
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero:
 You are a hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of a big hero and the product of Hamlet and Hamlet.
[Exeunt]

Scene IV: limit=floor(space/N)*N.
[Enter Prospero and Macbeth]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the quotient between Romeo and Juliet.
 You are as good as the product of yourself and Juliet.
[Exeunt]

Scene V: fixture-ൽ rejection ഉണ്ടായാൽ diagnostic zero; ഇല്ലെങ്കിൽ rank തുറക്കുന്നു.
[Enter Othello and Macbeth]
Othello:
 Am I better than Macbeth?
Macbeth:
 If so, let us proceed to scene VI.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between Othello and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Juliet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Open your heart.
 Let us proceed to scene VII.
[Exeunt]

Scene VI: unexpected rejection diagnostic.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero:
 You are nothing.
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

Scene VII: boundary probe പൂർത്തിയായി.
[Exeunt]
